msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Subtract</guilabel> mode</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial-select-layer.docbook:92
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now it's time to make the edges of the selection a bit fuzzy. This can be "
"done by applying <guilabel>Feather</guilabel> to the selection."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial-select-layer.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo><guilabel>Feather</guilabel> selection</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial-select-layer.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase><guilabel>Feather</guilabel> selection</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial-select-layer.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para><guilabel>Feather</guilabel> selection</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial-select-layer.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now cut the selection, using <menuchoice><guimenu>Edit</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Cut</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. Delete the current "
"layer with <menuchoice><guimenu>Layer</guimenu><guimenuitem>Remove Layer</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>. Paste your selection, with "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Paste</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice>. Now we give ourselves a bit more room to work in by resizing "
"the image a bit. Use the <menuchoice><guimenu>Image</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Change Image Size...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> dialog "
"for this."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial-select-layer.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Image Size</guilabel> dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial-select-layer.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Image Size</guilabel> dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial-select-layer.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Image Size</guilabel> dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial-select-layer.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Add a new layer, and place it below the old layer. You do this by selecting "
"the new layer in the layerbox, and then pressing the little 'down' arrow at "
"the bottom. Now we are going to select the area around the head with a "
"contiguous select (the tool has a selection-with-bucketfill icon at the "
"border)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial-select-layer.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Select Contiguous</guilabel> tool</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial-select-layer.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Select Contiguous</guilabel> tool</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial-select-layer.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Select Contiguous</guilabel> tool</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial-select-layer.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Make sure to select <guilabel>Sample merged</guilabel> in the tool options:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial-select-layer.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Sample merged</guilabel> option</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial-select-layer.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Sample merged</guilabel> option</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial-select-layer.docbook:167
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Sample merged</guilabel> option</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial-select-layer.docbook:171
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Feather the selection again, and invert it. Select the <guilabel>Contiguous "
"Fill</guilabel> tool (this is a different tool than the <guilabel>Contiguous "
"Select</guilabel> tool) and use it on the layer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial-select-layer.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Contiguous Fill</guilabel> tool</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial-select-layer.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Contiguous Fill</guilabel> tool</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial-select-layer.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The <guilabel>Contiguous Fill</guilabel> tool</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial-select-layer.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Deselect with <menuchoice><guimenu>Select</guimenu><guimenuitem>Deselect</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>. You'll notice some artifacts of the feathering at "
"the sides. You can select them easily with a rectangular selection and then "
"cut them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: tutorial-select-layer.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Select Rectangular</guilabel> tool</screeninfo>"
